ip">Mardavij ibn Ziyar was a Gilite military leader who founded the Ziyarid dynasty in northern Iran.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/mardin"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mardin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Mardin</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Mardin is a city in south-eastern Turkey, built in terraces on a steep hill overlooking the Mesopotamian plain.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/mardonius"><span class="enc-name">Mardonius</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Mardonius was a Persian general, nephew and son-in-law of Darius I.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/marduk"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/marduk.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Marduk</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">Marduk was the chief god of Babylon, elevated to head of the Mesopotamian pantheon as Babylon's power grew.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/marduk-kabit-ahheshu"><span class="enc-name">Marduk-kabit-ahheshu</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Marduk-kabit-ahheshu was the founder of the Second Dynasty of Isin, which ruled Babylonia from about 1157 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/marduk-nadin-ahhe"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/marduk-nadin-ahhe.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Marduk-nadin-ahhe</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Marduk-nadin-ahhe was a king of Babylon of the Second Dynasty of Isin, reigning from about 1099 to 1082 BCE, and a brother of Nebuchadnezzar I.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/marduk-zakir-shumi-i"><img class="enc-th